    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41-a1">

                <pb facs="0099" n="39" xml:id="pg39"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Garcia to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clarendon Hotel,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">New York,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 8, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>If, in order to your acceding to the intimation I have hinted at, it were
                    necessary to promise positively that the vessels which go from the United States
                    shall proceed on the route to Peru without attacking or provoking attacks from
                    other nations, without any exception, nor to cause injury nor to offer threats
                    to their possessions, I hold in pledge to the United States the honor of the
                    Peruvian government from this moment.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, with satisfaction, of this opportunity to renew to your
                    excellency the assurances of the high respect and esteem with which I subscribe
                    myself your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOSE ANTONIO G. Y GARCIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
